<section id="email" class="pub-card"><h2>Email reputation & delivery</h2><div class="google-actions"><form method="post" action="<?=url('/write/connections/google_postmaster/start')?>"><?=csrf_field()?><button class="wbtn">Connect Postmaster Tools</button></form><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="postmaster"><button class="wbtn">Read reputation report</button></form><a class="wbtn" href="<?=url('/write/mail-test')?>">Check owner email delivery</a><a class="wbtn" href="<?=url('/write/newsletter/templates')?>">Preview email templates</a></div><p>Workspace SMTP handles website messages. Gmail inbox access is not needed to send subscription and contact emails. Postmaster requires a verified sender domain and sufficient Gmail volume; missing data does not prove delivery failure.</p></section>
<section id="health" class="pub-card"><h2>Connection health</h2><div class="pub-table-wrap"><table class="pub-table"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Status</th><th>Last account verification (UTC)</th><th>Token expiry</th><th>Refresh</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($health as$h):?><tr><td><?=e($h['name'])?></td><td><?=e($h['status'])?></td><td><?=e($h['verified'])?></td><td><?=e($h['expiry'])?></td><td><?=e($h['refresh'])?><small>Refresh duration: <?=e($h['duration'])?></small></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div><p>“Connected” records authorization and destination confirmation; it does not guarantee the next API call will succeed. Run a report to verify access. Check Google Auth Platform publishing status: External apps in Testing commonly have seven-day refresh authorization.</p>
<h3>AI reporting through MCP</h3><p>The local Google MCP adapter reads saved aggregate audience reports, with no calendar events, drafts, credentials or live provider calls. A trusted MCP client must be configured by the operator. Google’s official Analytics MCP server is also available for a separately authorized analytics client. The public website does not expose an MCP endpoint.</p></section>
<section id="settings" class="pub-card"><h2>Google preferences</h2><form method="post"><?=csrf_field()?><input type="hidden" name="action" value="settings"><div class="google-grid"><?php foreach(['pagespeed_key'=>'PageSpeed API key','crux_key'=>'Chrome UX Report API key','picker_key'=>'Google Picker browser API key','gemini_key'=>'Gemini API key']as$key=>$label):?><div class="field"><label for="google-<?=e($key)?>"><?=e($label)?><?=setting('google.'.$key,'')!==''?' · saved':''?></label><input id="google-<?=e($key)?>" type="password" name="<?=e($key)?>" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="Leave blank to retain saved key"></div><?php endforeach;?><div class="field"><label>Gemini model<input name="gemini_model" value="<?=e(setting('google.gemini_model','gemini-3.8-flash'))?>" required></label></div><div class="field"><label>Public Google appointment booking link<input type="url" name="booking_url" value="<?=e(setting('google.booking_url',''))?>" placeholder="https://calendar.google.com/…"></label></div></div><button class="wbtn primary">Save Google preferences</button></form><p>The booking link appears on Contact once saved. Configure availability, buffers and Google Meet in Google Calendar. Connecting calendar read access alone does not create an appointment schedule.</p>
<details><summary>Google Cloud setup checklist</summary><p>Project: <strong>waithaka-ndegwa-website-512516</strong>. Keep the existing OAuth client and website hosting.</p><p>Enable Google Calendar API, YouTube Analytics API, Google Drive API, Google Picker API, Gmail Postmaster Tools API, PageSpeed Insights API and Chrome UX Report API as needed. Gemini requires its own API key and an appropriate data/billing tier. No billing account is activated by this website.</p><p>Add these exact authorized redirect URIs to the existing Web application client:</p><pre class="google-draft"><?php foreach(['google_calendar','google_youtube_analytics','google_drive','google_postmaster']as$s)echo e(url('/write/connections/callback/'.$s))."\n";?></pre><p>For Picker, restrict the browser key to this website’s HTTPS origin and Google Picker API. Use separate server keys restricted to their APIs. Add each account as an authorized test user if the app remains in Testing, or complete the applicable production setup and verification.</p></details></section>
